{"id": "EUVD-2026-85939", "enisaUuid": "cbe912c9-7706-345a-8326-c75d13439f53", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: harden DFS cache against invalid target hints\n\nCurrently, get_tgt_name() returns ERR_PTR(-ENOENT) when ce->tgthint is\nNULL, and dfs_cache_noreq_update_tgthint() assumes ce->tgthint is always\nvalid.\n\nIn preparation for clearing ce->tgthint in free_tgts(), harden callers\nof get_tgt_name() against ERR_PTR results and harden\ndfs_cache_noreq_update_tgthint() against NULL pointer dereferences.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:10:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:07:22", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a48328afbc3f63e3b9de8827e2e16c15b17976f7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6cb7f9fed8f40f28fbd464ca99c946951afc0952", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/66dbcdbb0cadffd12eb8f2b115fd57d384c5109d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/846f0709559b9e27024e126a80bc7afb76516912", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7e32da6047d9afdae8dd17b87b4c8d97363c4ee2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bf86c08123c6ab8c61cc0be1dad7540db93738ff"], "aliases": ["GHSA-whr7-9fmh-x37r", "CVE-2026-93210"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "13b86c65-380b-3ce7-a70c-a3536c402714", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "54be1f6c1c37498bba557049df646cc239fa37e3 <7e32da6047d9afdae8dd17b87b4c8d97363c4ee2"}, {"id": "1f760762-2610-3f4f-9019-2480a33418fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "499c0859-f734-3de9-bce4-b3bc0a1b6e18", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "54be1f6c1c37498bba557049df646cc239fa37e3 <66dbcdbb0cadffd12eb8f2b115fd57d384c5109d"}, {"id": "61330c01-7815-3498-b261-fabeaaa8dda2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "82eaae66-4661-3564-a8cf